From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 07:24:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 21 Oct launch: one address lets a hundred people sign up at
 once

The tester's 61646 (D787) and Misho, 16 Oct: about a hundred people join
through one invitation link, most on mobile data, where a carrier puts many
phones behind one address, the rest on one room's Wi-Fi.

- GET /invite-codes/:code allowed 20 checks a minute per address, so the
  twenty-first person in the same minute was turned away at the join page.
- /auth/* allowed 300 calls per address in five minutes. One sign-up is six
  or seven calls (referral opened, eligibility, OTP, verify, register,
  complete), so a hundred at once is about 700.

Both now allow 1,500 per address in five minutes. The per-person caps (30
auth calls, 5 SMS) are unchanged, and codes are 8 random characters.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
